<title>UK: Fire alarm disrupts LIFFE commodity trading.</title>
<headline>Fire alarm disrupts LIFFE commodity trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Floor trading in LIFFE commodity products was disrupted by a fire alarm this morning, a LIFFE spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The exchange's Commodity Quay building had to be evacuated after an alarm which sounded at 0925 GMT, the spokeswoman said. Contracts re-opened at 1005 GMT.</p>
<p>Screen based trading in white sugar futures was unaffected, traders said.</p>
<p>There was no fire, a building security officer said.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
